    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "For consecutive replicators A and B joined through a port with delta d, B is known unpaired when 0 ≤ lB − lA ≤ d. In the paper’s reading, B cannot interact before A is annihilated—and since A is unpaired, that never happens. The inequality is a safety proof, not a performance hint.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000345"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0005-flat-03",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "Before: two-agent replicator tree",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000346"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0005-flat-03",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "flowchart TB\nrootM((root))\nA[\"A · unpaired · ℓ = 2\"]\nlive[\"endpoint ℓ = 2\"]\nB[\"B · ℓ = 4\"]\nb1[\"endpoint ℓ = 3\"]\nb2[\"endpoint ℓ = 6\"]\nrootM --> A\nA -->|d = 0| live\nA -->|d = 3| B\nB --> b1\nB --> b2",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000347"
      ],
      "defines": [],
